verdicts.fix_notes:
**Preferred fix: work out the change part when the history is read.** This follows the owner's rule that the most private option is the default. It adds no request and keeps nothing new, so the 18 November policy entry needs no change.

In activity.ts `classOf`, after `const stored = readClass(entry.origin)`:

```ts
const SPENDS = new Set(["transfer", "withdraw", "mint", "remove", "lovejoin-launch"]);
if (stored && SPENDS.has(entry.kind)) {
  const ps = stored.id.split("+");
  if (!ps.some((p) => p.startsWith("change:")) && !ps.some((p) => p === "public" || p.startsWith("public:")))
    return merged([stored, leftBy(entry.txHash)]);
}
```

**The `public:` guard is required; the finding's sketch doesn't have it.** A new Make public paid only to the user's own accounts stores `public:<n>+…` with no `change:` part (withdraw.ts:152-166 `tiedBy`). Testing for a missing `change:` part alone would therefore re-class new entries too: own#1's Own rank (Mint 4, Fund 4) would become Session 5, and they'd gain a Change tag.

The guard also leaves these as they are, and they already rank after money others paid and after boxes, so :171 holds for them:
- account mints (`madePrivate` alone);
- old spends paid from money the user made private (Own 4).

Other points:
- No "from" check is needed for lovejoin-launch: only private launches enter the Seedelf history (activity.ts:379).
- Leave entries with no stored origin as UNKNOWN (rank 3, after money others paid).
- session-out and session-back entries aren't spend kinds, so they're untouched.
- An old Make public to the user's own account will read as Change rather than as that account. That is safe, since it still ranks after money others paid. Say so in architecture.md:151 and in the histories.ts:34-39 comment ("entries written before get the part on read").
- The same change fixes the box-paid case.

**Alternative, if the owner prefers no read-time logic:** keep the code and qualify privacy.md:171 and architecture.md:151 the way :172 qualifies boxes. For example: "…once the wallet notes that tie; change from before keeps its inputs' histories alone, so change from a payment received still ranks, and is tagged, as received money."

1. **Fix withdrawOne** (lovejoin.ts:8146-8172). A deposit's answer that was kept without its inputs, and that no record names, can't say whose deposit it was. Its way back should be Unknown, never Received. This prototype was tried in the copy:
```ts
const blindOf = (x: Schedule) => {
  const o = x.origins?.[box.txHash];
  return !!o && !o.public && o.inputs === undefined && mixedFor(o, poolOf(box)) === false && !depositsNamed(x).has(box.txHash);
};
const received = !blindOf(before) && (await this.someoneElses(network, before, [box])).length > 0;
// inside the update, the Unknown branch:
: blindOf(s) || (!knownOf(s)(box) && !depositsNamed(s).has(box.txHash))
  ? unknownIn(built.txHash)
```
   - The origin is then written already, because `own.origin` isn't "lovejoin" (:8178).
   - Only the retired pools' way back changes. In a current pool a blind answer never reaches withdrawOne, because rejudge deletes it first.
   - Leave someoneElsesOf as it is. For Mix my boxes again, counting the answer as someone else's is the safe side: the box is left out. Reword its comment at :2728-2729 to say the box comes back as Unknown.
   - If l2time#1 changes what class a box the wallet can't place gets, use that class here too.
   - With the prototype applied:
     - the new test passes;
     - the 9 nearest suites pass (146 tests);
     - 63 files on Lovejoin, the hatch, histories, minting, restores and withdraws pass (1037 tests). restore-scan's two 5-second timeouts happened under load average 33 and passed when run alone;
     - `tsc --noEmit` is clean.
